HST Office (1.0.2 ribbon, approved mockup): the compact ribbon (Ctrl+F1), its dropped page and the quick
access toolbar as the mockup draws them.

Quick row: 30 px buttons (icon 16 and the label beside it), 1 x 22 px separators with 4 px on each side, the
first button 6 px from the left edge, centred in the 45 px row; ˅ (18 x 16) 4 px from the row's lower right.
Dropped page (a tab clicked in the compact state): 106 px between two 3 px strips, the width the tab control
gives (W - 276 with the banner 8 px from both sides), the groups choosing their state for that width; the pin
˅ at its lower right brings the full ribbon back; Esc, a click outside, a command or the same tab close it; a
click on another tab drops that tab's page. The quick access toolbar shows New, Open, Save, Undo, Redo and
Print (owner decision D3, replacing the three-button default of 14/11) in the four apps, KeyTips 1 to 6 by
position; New (.uno:AddDirect, Ctrl+N) is a plain button without its document type ▾; profiles with a
customised toolbar keep it. The quick row's Tìm is the find bar (Ctrl+F) as on the ribbon; the find bar and HST
commands take the 16 px icon their ribbon button shows (data/ribbon/quick-rows.json "icons").

